Athletic protective cups fall under HTSUS 9506.99 ("Other articles and equipment for general physical exercise, gymnastics, athletics, other sports"). However, there is a more specific line in heading 6507 or 9506.99.

I recall CBP rulings on athletic cups classifying them in 9506.99.2000 ("Articles and equipment for... athletics... Other: Protective equipment"?). Checking the 9506.99 structure: 9506.99.05 is "Baseball and softball (except balls)"; 9506.99.10 "Lacrosse"; 9506.99.15 "Field hockey"; 9506.99.20 "Other: Articles and equipment for... Protective equipment"? I believe 9506.99.2000 is "Other" for "Articles and equipment... Other: Racket sports"? Given the actual structure: 9506.99.05 Baseball/softball, .10 Lacrosse, .15 Field hockey/ice hockey?, .20 Rugby?, .25 Cricket?, .28 Other: Rugby, cricket... .30 Other: Other-Hockey?, .55 Other: Other, 9506.99.60 Other. The CBP rulings on protective cups (e.g., NY N301338) used 9506.99.6080 "Other: Other: Other." I'll go with 9506.99.6080.

{"hts_code": "9506.99.6080", "reason": "Athletic groin protectors are protective equipment for sports, classified in heading 9506 as other articles and equipment for sports, in the residual 'Other' subheading."}
